Id: int001w
Severity: WARN
Category: integrity
Check: check_integrity
Fix: Build the database (aide --init) and move it into place.
References: aide.conf(5)
Controls: NIST SI-7; ISO 8.16

AIDE is configured but its database was never built: it
compares against nothing. The database is the one aide.conf says
AIDE reads (database_in, or database in AIDE before 0.16), with
its @@define macros and included files followed; it is missing or
empty. 'aide --init' writes a new database where database_out
points, and it does nothing until it is moved to database_in.
Initialize it, or take AIDE out.
